<title>BRAZIL: Brazil govt sells 64 percent in coffee stock sale.</title>
<headline>Brazil govt sells 64 percent in coffee stock sale.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Brazilian government sold 128,005 bags, or 63.97 percent of the 200,090 60-kg bags of coffee stocks offered to all segments of the coffee sector in its auction today, said an official from the Banco do Brasil.</p>
<p>Total revenue for the government was just over 18.50 million reais ($17.45 million).</p>
